Files that carry an "Adapted from" or copyright header keep that header.

Third-party work included or built upon:

- Rockbox (https://github.com/Rockbox/rockbox): bootloader, dual-boot
  installer, hardware drivers, the crossfeed filters, the channel modes and the
  compressor. GPL-2.0-or-later.
- wInd3x (https://github.com/freemyipod/wInd3x) by Serge "q3k" Bazanski:
  BootROM DFU exploit, DFU protocol and payload assembler, ported from Go to
  Rust. GPL-2.0-or-later.
- Cupertino Icons (https://github.com/flutter/packages): the Settings glyphs
  and the Flat theme's artwork. MIT.
- Inter (https://github.com/rsms/inter): the numerals of the Flat theme's
  artwork. SIL OFL 1.1.
- The Flat theme's design follows "My own iPodOS edits" by u/DrawingCompetitive76
  on r/IpodClassic (https://www.reddit.com/r/IpodClassic/comments/1x2856t/my_own_ipodos_edits/).

Apple firmware is never included. Builds read it from the user's own IPSW.
